## Milestone Rules

Based on the scene design and common-sense feedback, here are the milestone completion criteria:

```json
{
  "milestones": [
    {
      "id": "find_gray_concrete_powder",
      "task": "find gray_concrete_powder",
      "description": "Player locates and looks at the gray concrete powder pillar structure",
      "rules": [
        {
          "type": "position_near_with_facing",
          "target": [3, 1, 3],
          "max_distance": 5,
          "facing_tolerance": 60,
          "description": "Player is within 5 blocks of the gray concrete powder pillar and facing it"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "find_target",
      "task": "find target",
      "description": "Player locates and looks at the target block column",
      "rules": [
        {
          "type": "position_near_with_facing",
          "target": [6, 1, 3],
          "max_distance": 5,
          "facing_tolerance": 60,
          "description": "Player is within 5 blocks of the target column and facing it"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mine_cobblestone_wall",
      "task": "mine cobblestone_wall",
      "description": "Player mines at least one cobblestone wall block and collects it",
      "rules": [
        {
          "type": "inventory_has",
          "item": "cobblestone_wall",
          "min_count": 1,
          "description": "Player has at least 1 cobblestone_wall in inventory from mining the wall structure"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Design Notes:
- **find gray_concrete_powder**: Uses `position_near_with_facing` centered on the pillar's middle block (~3, ~1, ~3). Max distance of 5 blocks ensures the player has actually navigated to it, not just spawned nearby. 60° facing tolerance is generous enough to account for looking at any part of the structure.
- **find target**: Same approach, centered on the target column at (~6, ~1, ~3). The 5-block distance ensures the player moved from the concrete powder area toward the target.
- **mine cobblestone_wall**: Uses `inventory_has` checking for `cobblestone_wall` item (NOT `cobblestone`, per CommonSenseAgent's advice). The wooden pickaxe is provided and sufficient to mine this block. The 3×3×3 wall mass gives 27 blocks to mine, so getting at least 1 is very achievable.

